wa — A personal WhatsApp account from the command line, as a linked device, for agents and scripts

Usage: wa <profile> <command> [options]
Account commands start with your profile, a name you choose; none is ever assumed.

Works with:
  tg                      Telegram in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  max                     MAX in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  zm                      Zoom meetings: transcripts and summaries, searchable with your other WireCat data
  drive                   Google Drive and Docs as local text, searchable with your other WireCat data
  gcal                    Google Calendar events, searchable with your other WireCat data
  memo context <person>   one person across messengers, mail, notes and meetings
  mail                    IMAP mail in the same local store: search your mailbox offline, next to your other WireCat data

Start here:   wa personal setup  (any profile name works)
              wa account list    your profiles and their logged-in accounts
Next:         wa commands        every command, by section
              wa help options    output, offline, timeouts, dry run
For agents:   wa skill show      rules and the discovery loop

Getting started after installation:
  wa personal setup               Guided first run as profile personal; about 5 minutes
  wa personal setup --agent codex Link and install your agent's skill
  wa setup --help                 Linking choices and examples
Every account command names its profile first: `wa personal chats list`.

For agents:
  wa skill show                   Read the bundled instructions before using WhatsApp
  wa commands --json              Discover commands, arguments and flags

